BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

MAYOR OF GORONTALO,

Considering:
a. that Pancasila and the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia guarantee the right of every citizen to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and to obtain a sense of security and freedom from all forms of violence;
b. that all forms of acts of violence against women and children constitute violations of human rights so that their self-worth and dignity need to be protected and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their nature and disposition without discrimination;
c. that women's empowerment and child protection are concurrent governmental affairs delegated to the regions to become the basis for implementing regional autonomy and become mandatory governmental affairs not related to basic services as referred to in Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government;
d. that in order to provide regulatory strengthening, direction, and foundation in the protection of women and children victims of violence, regulation or regulations related to the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence are required;

2 -
e. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, letter c, letter d, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;

In View of:
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

