CHAPTER 111

RIGHTS OF VICTIMS

Article 12

Every Victim obtains the right:
a. to be respected for their dignity and worth as a human being;
b. recovery of health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by the victim;
c. to determine their own decisions;
d. to obtain information;
e. confidentiality of their identity;
f. compensation;
g. social rehabilitation;
h. complaint handling;

i. to obtain facilitation in the judicial process; and/or  j. assistance.

